ink you know reasonable people can  disagree on that and I think maybe we do  going back to the taxation part where  would you set the top marginal tax rate  and and what would it be in other words  would it be 40 percent above a million  dollars a year or where would you set  that well we cut detect the corporate  tax rate down to 14 and then or sorry  the I think 21 and now I'm suggesting we  go up to 25 percent which is still a  reduction downward but it's higher than  this bill and this  new law has put into place and I think  getting some adjustment on the corporate  rate is reasonable I just think that it  went way too far at the expense of  working people and I may have been  unclear in my quote I mean when it comes  to the individual tax rate would you  raise the top tax rate and if so where  would you set it and what would be the  income threshold so I think that's  negotiable where and how because we are  seeing different levels for the very  wealthy down to those of us in great  need so I would be willing to work  through that particular issue and and  see where we can land where we actually  see a decrease or an increase of the  rate for those at the highest level and  we are giving some benefit back to  especially those working-class people  who are working day to day in and out  trying to to make it what would be the I  mean I'm just trying to understand under  so I think the numbers do sort of  indicate sort of what your philosophy is  what would be middle class what would be  the upper income limit for somebody  who's middle class who you'd be  targeting and trying to help so I think  what I what I'm really saying is that  people who are you know making forty  fifty sixty thousand dollars a year in  the state of Utah need a break and  that's the rate where I think we need to  be the most aware and pay you know and  and and give some tax relief to that  middle worker who is out there working  you know our in our on our ranches who  is working in our convenience stores  who's working you know a job where they  get up every day and do their thing and  many of them working several so that's  that's the kind of mid-level rate that  I'm looking to provide relief to all  right we have been speaking with Jenny  Wilson two terms Salt Lake County  Council member currently running against  Republican candidate for US Senate Mitt  Romney she is the Democratic nominee you  can learn more about her campaign at  Wilson for senate.com Jenny we're going  to be following it and best of luck to  you well I appreciate I appreciate the  opportunity to speak with you for a few  minutes today

